    body: [
      { t: "img", src: "assets/img/news/tibet-fieldwork-20261020/wx2-02.jpg", caption: "日照金山，珠穆朗玛 Mount Everest illuminated by golden morning sun" },
      { t: "p", text: "清华大学深圳国际研究生院未来人居数字引擎实验室（TiDE Lab）师生及合作团队前往西藏，围绕喜马拉雅未来中心开展实地调研与交流。此次行程以城乡联动的「未来零售」为主题，结合当地生态环境、乡村可持续发展与在地文化传承，探讨深度设计、数字技术与新型未来零售模式在喜马拉雅地区应用的可能。" },
      { t: "en", text: "Researchers and students from TiDE Lab at Tsinghua Shenzhen International Graduate School (SIGS), together with collaborating teams, visited Tibet for field research and exchange activities related to the Himalayan Future Center. Themed around rural-urban reciprocal \"Future Retail\", the trip explored how deep design, digital technology, and new retail models might apply in the Himalayan region, in connection with local ecology, rural sustainability, and cultural heritage." },
      { t: "img", src: "assets/img/news/tibet-fieldwork-20261020/wx2-01.jpg", caption: "TiDE Lab 合照 TiDE Lab Group Photo" },
      { t: "p", text: "调研期间，团队走访了珠峰脚下巴松村周边地区，近距离感受高原地区的自然环境与当地生活场景。与城市中的零售形态不同，高原乡村在地理条件、基础设施、文化传统、品牌价值和文旅消费群体行为与需求等方面具有自身特点。这些差异也为未来零售课题如何建立「喜马拉雅+」的全新模式提供了新的研究视角。" },
      { t: "en", text: "During the visit, the team travelled through villages including Basong at the bottom of Mount Everest, observing the natural landscape and everyday life of the Tibetan Plateau. Compared with urban retail environments, plateau villages have their own characteristics in geography, infrastructure, cultural tradition, brand value, and tourist-consumption behaviour — offering new research perspectives for building a \"Himalaya+\" model of future retail." },
      { t: "img", src: "assets/img/news/tibet-fieldwork-20261020/wx2-03.jpg", caption: "当地建筑、乡村环境及项目调研 Local Architecture and Field Observations" },
      { t: "p", text: "喜马拉雅未来零售项目关注数字技术、空间设计与乡村发展的结合，希望探索适应当地环境与生活需求的新型零售空间和服务模式。项目不仅关注零售空间本身，也希望进一步思考零售活动与地方文化、社区生活及乡村经济之间的关系。此次实地走访为后续研究提供了来自真实场景的观察与参考。" },
      { t: "en", text: "The Himalayan Future Retail Project focuses on integrating digital technologies, spatial innovation, and rural-urban reciprocal development, aiming to explore new sustainable retail spaces and business models adapted to local environments and living needs. Beyond retail space itself, the project also considers the relationship between retail activity, local culture, community life, and rural economy." },
      { t: "img", src: "assets/img/news/tibet-fieldwork-20261020/wx2-04.jpg", caption: "高原调研 Field Research on the Plateau" },
      { t: "p", text: "此次活动得到了多方合作伙伴的支持。感谢吉山吉舍的多吉、央金夫妇，长期参与当地乡村实践的周利老师、李文老师，以及天鸿集团等伙伴对活动的支持。同时，沈振江院士带领的福州大学国际联合智慧营造实验室，以及清华大学深圳国际研究生院王学谦教授机器人研究团队，也参与了项目的跨学科研发合作。" },
      { t: "en", text: "The visit was supported by partners from different fields, including Dorje and Yangjin of Jishan Jishe, rural development practitioners Zhou Li and Li Wen, Tianhong Group, and others. The International Joint Laboratory for Smart Construction at Fuzhou University led by Prof. Shen Zhenjiang, as well as the robotics research team of Prof. Wang Xueqian at Tsinghua SIGS, also participated in the interdisciplinary R&D collaboration." },
      { t: "p", text: "此次西藏之行是喜马拉雅未来中心项目探索过程中的一次实地实践。未来，TiDE Lab 将继续结合数字技术、设计研究与真实场景需求，推进相关研究与实验，探索面向未来城乡生活的更多可能。" },
      { t: "en", text: "The visit to Tibet formed part of the ongoing exploration of the Himalayan Future Center Project. Moving forward, TiDE Lab will continue to connect digital technologies and design research with real-world needs, advancing related research and experiments for future urban-rural life." }
    ]
